",[504],{"title":505,"path":506,"stem":507},"Loading Indicator","\u002Fdocs\u002Fweb\u002Fnuxt\u002Floading-indicator","1.docs\u002Fweb\u002Fnuxt\u002Floading-indicator",{"title":509,"icon":510,"path":511,"stem":512,"children":513,"page":22},"Tiptap","i-mdi-file-edit-outline","\u002Fdocs\u002Fweb\u002Ftiptap","1.docs\u002Fweb\u002Ftiptap",[514],{"title":515,"path":516,"stem":517},"Snippets","\u002Fdocs\u002Fweb\u002Ftiptap\u002Fsnippets","1.docs\u002Fweb\u002Ftiptap\u002Fsnippets",{"id":519,"title":520,"authors":521,"badge":527,"body":528,"date":876,"description":877,"extension":878,"image":879,"meta":880,"navigation":885,"path":886,"seo":887,"stem":888,"__hash__":889},"posts\u002F3.blog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup.md","My New Home Office Setup",[522],{"name":523,"to":524,"avatar":525},"Alexander Trost","https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fgalexrt",{"src":526},"\u002Fimages\u002Fprofile-picture.webp",null,{"type":529,"value":530,"toc":858},"minimark",[531,535,540,543,546,550,555,558,580,583,592,596,599,602,625,628,632,635,638,642,655,658,694,697,701,710,719,722,725,742,746,749,793,796,800,809,812,816,825,829,832,839,845,848,852,855],[532,533,534],"p",{},"In this post I'm going over my new game and home office setup.",[536,537,539],"h2",{"id":538},"new-table","New table",[532,541,542],{},"First part of the new home setup, was a new table.\nThe previous was a cheap table from IKEA. The new table is 2.60m long instead of previously only 2.00m.\nThe 0.60m more space is awesome. The desk feels emptier but in a good way, and I have more space for equipment.",[532,544,545],{},"If you have the space, go for a big table and keep it clean!",[536,547,549],{"id":548},"tech-stuff","Tech stuff",[551,552,554],"h3",{"id":553},"power-distribution","Power Distribution",[532,556,557],{},"The following power strips are used for power distribution:",[559,560,561,572],"ul",{},[562,563,564,565],"li",{},"2x ",[566,567,571],"a",{"href":568,"rel":569},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fintl\u002Fadam_hall_874716_power_strip_1_u_19.htm",[570],"nofollow","Adam Hall 874716 Power Strip 1 U 19\" - 16-port",[562,573,574,575],{},"And some ",[566,576,579],{"href":577,"rel":578},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fintl\u002Fthe_t_racks_power_8_s.htm",[570],"the t.racks Power 8 S - 8-port",[532,581,582],{},"The 16-port power strips are pretyy neat and I can recommend them.\n(I'll soon \"mount\" them to the table so that the cables are off the ground)",[532,584,585,586,591],{},"End goal here would be to finally buy myself a fancy ",[566,587,590],{"href":588,"rel":589},"https:\u002F\u002Fen.wikipedia.org\u002Fwiki\u002FUninterruptible_power_supply",[570],"Uninterruptible power supply",", just in case the apocalypse is happening :-D",[551,593,595],{"id":594},"network","Network",[532,597,598],{},"I'm driving a dual WAN setup using a FritzBoxes and a OpenSense firewall router.",[532,600,601],{},"OpenSense firewall router box hardware specifications:",[559,603,604,607,610,613,616,619,622],{},[562,605,606],{},"CPU: Intel Celeron G4900",[562,608,609],{},"Fan: Noctua NH-L9x65 CPU-Kühler",[562,611,612],{},"RAM: Crucial Ballistix DDR4-2666 4GB",[562,614,615],{},"Mainboard: Gigabyte B360N WIFI",[562,617,618],{},"PSU: Kolink SFX-350",[562,620,621],{},"Sorage: Samsung 860 EVO 260GB SSD",[562,623,624],{},"Case: Kolink - Satellite Mini-ITX-\u002F Micro-ATX-Gehäuse - schwarz",[532,626,627],{},"For network switches, I'm using two cheap 8-port Netgear Managed Switches which get the job done (they can VLAN so perfect with my OpenSense firewall router).",[551,629,631],{"id":630},"automation","Automation",[532,633,634],{},"I have a few Raspberry Pis which power the video surveillance and security system, and take care of home automations, like turning on the lights in the morning and so on.",[532,636,637],{},"I can probably extend this, but I'm fine with what it does right now.",[551,639,641],{"id":640},"computers","Computers",[643,644,645,652],"blockquote",{},[532,646,647,648,651],{},"The most important part of the calculation are the ",[649,650,640],"del",{}," calculators.",[532,653,654],{},"- Alexander Trost",[532,656,657],{},"I have two machines, one for gaming and one for working:",[559,659,660,677],{},[562,661,662,663],{},"Gaming\n",[559,664,665,668,671,674],{},[562,666,667],{},"CPU: Intel(c) I7-7700k",[562,669,670],{},"Memory: 16GB DDR4-3000",[562,672,673],{},"GPU: Nvidia GeForce GTX 970",[562,675,676],{},"Disk(s): 1x 500GB SATA SSD, 1x 3TB SATA HDD, 1x 4TB SATA HDD",[562,678,679,680],{},"Workstation\n",[559,681,682,685,688,691],{},[562,683,684],{},"CPU: AMD Ryzen 7 1800X",[562,686,687],{},"Memory: 32GB DDR4-2133",[562,689,690],{},"GPU: 2x Radeon RX 560 OC 4G",[562,692,693],{},"Disk(s): 1x 500GB NVMe SSD, 1x 500GB SATA SSD",[532,695,696],{},"Obviously the gaming computer can always need an upgrade but I am happy with it and the workstation.\nYou really notice the 8 cores and 16 threads of the AMD Ryzen when compiling code.",[551,698,700],{"id":699},"monitors","Monitors",[532,702,703,704,709],{},"I'm currently using 4x LG 29UM68-P 29\" 21:9 UltraWide LED monitors, see ",[566,705,708],{"href":706,"rel":707},"http:\u002F\u002Fwww.lg.com\u002Fus\u002Fmonitors\u002Flg-29UM68-P-ultrawide-monitor",[570],"LG 29UM68-P 29\" product page",".",[532,711,712,713,718],{},"A big shoutout to ",[566,714,717],{"href":715,"rel":716},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ricoo.eu\u002F",[570],"Ricoo Medientechnik"," for their awesome and not too expensive* monitor stands!",[532,720,721],{},"(*In comparsion with around 4 other companies that sell and\u002F or buy monitor stands)",[532,723,724],{},"I'm using the following monitor stands from Ricoo:",[559,726,727,735],{},[562,728,729,730],{},"1x ",[566,731,734],{"href":732,"rel":733},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ricoo.eu\u002Fen\u002Fricoo-pc-screen-led-monitor-stand-ts3511-table-mount-for-2-monitors-monitor-brackets-tft-swivel-arm-monitor-mount-pivoting-monitor-fastener-monitor-rack-monitor-arm-compatible-with-vesa-100x100\u002Fa-11189\u002F",[570],"Ricoo Monitor Stand TS3511 Table Mount for 2 Monitors (TS3011)",[562,736,564,737],{},[566,738,741],{"href":739,"rel":740},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.ricoo.eu\u002Fen\u002Fricoo-desk-mount-monitor-ts3011-with-gas-spring-articulation-monitor-bracket-swivelling-tiltable-desk-monitor-stand-pedestal-flat-screen-pc-monitor-tft-display-swivel-arm-desk-led-lcd-desk-holder-brackets-universal-tv-vesa-75x75-100x100\u002Fa-10789\u002F",[570],"Ricoo Desk Monitor Mount Arm (TS3011)",[551,743,745],{"id":744},"audio","Audio",[532,747,748],{},"Moving on to the audio equipment, I use the following pieces for audio input and output control:",[559,750,751,765,772,785],{},[562,752,753,758,759,764],{},[566,754,757],{"href":755,"rel":756},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fde\u002Fdbx_286_s.htm",[570],"DBX 286 S"," (Temporarily switched out for ",[566,760,763],{"href":761,"rel":762},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fgb\u002Fbehringer_xenyx_802.htm",[570],"Behringer 802 Xenyx",")",[562,766,767],{},[566,768,771],{"href":769,"rel":770},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fde\u002Frode_nt1a_complete_vocal_recording.htm",[570],"Rode NT1-A Complete Vocal Recording",[562,773,774,779,780,764],{},[566,775,778],{"href":776,"rel":777},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.thomann.de\u002Fgb\u002Fnumark_m_4_black.htm",[570],"Numark M 4"," (The link is to the black edition, but I have the grey one. I got it cheap from ",[566,781,784],{"href":782,"rel":783},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.rockshop.de\u002F",[570],"Rockshop.de",[562,786,787,792],{},[566,788,791],{"href":789,"rel":790},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.rockshop.de\u002Fakai-mpx8",[570],"Akai MPX8"," (Just for the lolz as a soundboard style \"player\")",[532,794,795],{},"To \"blast\" music at the neighbors I have a very old 5.1 sound system, which sadly has a high level of noise by default. I'll probably replace it soon with a better sound system.",[551,797,799],{"id":798},"chair","Chair",[532,801,802,803,808],{},"A ",[566,804,807],{"href":805,"rel":806},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.caseking.de\u002Fnoblechairs-epic-gaming-stuhl-schwarz-gold-gagc-038.html",[570],"noblechairs EPIC Gaming Stuhl - schwarz\u002Fgold"," because your arse and back will thank you for it.",[532,810,811],{},"Pretty good chair, though if you want to spend more go for a more expensive one with, e.g., \"limitless\" backrest and more features.",[536,813,815],{"id":814},"finishing-touches","Finishing touches",[532,817,818,819,824],{},"To give the whole setup a nice touch, I have added ",[566,820,823],{"href":821,"rel":822},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.amazon.de\u002FPhilips-LightStrip-erweiterbar-Millionen-kompatibel\u002Fdp\u002FB0148NMVQA",[570],"Philipps Hue LED Lightstrips"," to the back of the monitors. Though I still have to finally use the \"in-built\" glue of the light strips to put them on the back of the monitors.",[536,826,828],{"id":827},"result","Result",[532,830,831],{},"The result is pretty rad!",[532,833,834],{},[835,836],"img",{"alt":837,"src":838},"My New Home Setup - Rad Results!","\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup\u002Fhomeoffice-desktop-setup-shot-1.jpg",[532,840,841],{},[835,842],{"alt":843,"src":844},"My New Home Setup - With colored background lighting even better!","\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup\u002Fhomeoffice-desktop-setup-shot-2.jpg",[532,846,847],{},"(The LightStrip is hanging down as this was a picture during me gluing it to the monitors with the integrated glue strips)",[536,849,851],{"id":850},"summary","Summary",[532,853,854],{},"That is my home office setup. It gets the job done and is a dream come true for me.\nI have more ideas to exapnd this setup, e.g., making cut outs for the mixer, but I have to see if I'm going that far.",[532,856,857],{},"Have Fun!",{"title":859,"searchDepth":860,"depth":860,"links":861},"",2,[862,863,873,874,875],{"id":538,"depth":860,"text":539},{"id":548,"depth":860,"text":549,"children":864},[865,867,868,869,870,871,872],{"id":553,"depth":866,"text":554},3,{"id":594,"depth":866,"text":595},{"id":630,"depth":866,"text":631},{"id":640,"depth":866,"text":641},{"id":699,"depth":866,"text":700},{"id":744,"depth":866,"text":745},{"id":798,"depth":866,"text":799},{"id":814,"depth":860,"text":815},{"id":827,"depth":860,"text":828},{"id":850,"depth":860,"text":851},"2018-06-05T13:47:13+02:00","In this post I'm showing you my new gaming and home office setup.","md",{"src":838},{"tags":881},[882,883,884,641],"Home","Office","Setup",true,"\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup",{"title":520,"description":877},"3.blog\u002F2018\u002Fmy-new-home-office-setup","VUxxMS3M49a1KwnEnGGMTyLo3sjLUnAjP-Qhpdxz9_0",[891,896],{"title":892,"path":893,"stem":894,"description":895,"children":-1},"KubeCon Copenhagen 2018 - Day 3","\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fkubecon-copenhagen-2018-day-3","3.blog\u002F2018\u002Fkubecon-copenhagen-2018-day-3","Talks, keynotes, thoughts and pictures from the KubeCon Copenhagen 2018 Day 3.",{"title":897,"path":898,"stem":899,"description":900,"children":-1},"What exactly is „Cloud Native\" even?","\u002Fblog\u002F2018\u002Fwhat-exactly-is-cloud-native-even","3.blog\u002F2018\u002Fwhat-exactly-is-cloud-native-even","Cross-Post of my \"What exactly is „Cloud Native\" even?\" article from \"The Cloud Report\"",1793388882980]